{
  "id": "cb11",
  "title": "PERFORM VARYING",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "cb11-l1",
      "title": "Counting Loops",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "PERFORM SHOW-LINE VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 5 is COBOL's counting loop: I starts at 1, goes up by 1 after each round, and the loop stops once I is above 5.",
        "BY can be any step: BY 2 counts 1, 3, 5. FROM 10 BY -1 UNTIL I < 1 counts down.",
        "After the loop, I holds the first value that stopped it: 6 in the first example."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. VARY.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 I         PIC 99.",
          "       01 SQUARE    PIC 999.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "       MAIN.",
          "           PERFORM SHOW-SQUARE VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 5.",
          "           DISPLAY \"I AFTER THE LOOP: \" I.",
          "           STOP RUN.",
          "       SHOW-SQUARE.",
          "           COMPUTE SQUARE = I * I.",
          "           DISPLAY I \" SQUARED IS \" SQUARE."
        ],
        "output": [
          "01 SQUARED IS 001",
          "02 SQUARED IS 004",
          "03 SQUARED IS 009",
          "04 SQUARED IS 016",
          "05 SQUARED IS 025",
          "I AFTER THE LOOP: 06"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
