    {
      "id": "cb11-l3",
      "title": "Loops in Loops",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "VARYING can count two things at once: VARYING ROW FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL ROW > 3 AFTER COL FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL COL > 3. For every ROW, COL runs through all its values.",
        "It's the same as an inline PERFORM inside another one, and both styles are common.",
        "The example builds a small multiplication table, one line per row, with STRING-free tricks: WITH NO ADVANCING."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. TABLE.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 R-NO     PIC 9.",
          "       01 C-NO     PIC 9.",
          "       01 PRODUCT  PIC Z9.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           PERFORM VARYING R-NO FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL R-NO > 3",
          "               PERFORM VARYING C-NO FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL C-NO > 4",
          "                   COMPUTE PRODUCT = R-NO * C-NO",
          "                   DISPLAY PRODUCT \" \" WITH NO ADVANCING",
          "               END-PERFORM",
          "               DISPLAY \" \"",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          " 1  2  3  4  ",
          " 2  4  6  8  ",
          " 3  6  9 12  "
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
